            <ArticleTitle>Tuberculous peritonitis presenting as an acute abdomen: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e11-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajog.2011.01.039</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Female genital tuberculosis is relatively rare and difficult to diagnose. Often it is mistaken for ovarian malignancy. We report a case of a young immigrant woman with acute abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
